OVERVIEW: Link a Swift Package product to a target

Links an existing Swift Package product to a target. The package must already
be added to the project. Use this when you need to link a package to additional
targets after initial setup.

Examples:
  xcodeproj-cli link-package-product Alamofire --target MyApp
  xcodeproj-cli link-package-product RealmSwift --target MyApp --package
https://github.com/realm/realm-swift.git

USAGE: xcodeproj-cli link-package-product [--project <project>] [--workspace <workspace>] [--verbose] [--dry-run] <product-name> --target <target> [--package <package>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <product-name>          Name of the package product to link (e.g.,
                          'Alamofire')

OPTIONS:
  -p, --project <project> Path to .xcodeproj file (default: looks for
                          *.xcodeproj in current directory)
  -w, --workspace <workspace>
                          Path to .xcworkspace file
  -V, --verbose           Enable verbose output with performance metrics
  --dry-run               Preview changes without saving
  -t, --target <target>   Target to link the package product to
  --package <package>     Package URL for disambiguation when product name
                          doesn't match package URL
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

